    "text": "<p>The figure shows a region of length &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math>&#39; with a uniform magnetic field of&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> in it and a proton entering the region with velocity&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> making an angle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>&nbsp;with the field. If the proton completes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math>&nbsp;revolution by the time it cross the region shown, &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math>&#39; is close to (mass of proton <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>67</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>, charge of the proton<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>)</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/95fed626-5d44-4c80-adec-d80165777532-image.png\" style=\"width: 201px; height: 174px;\" />&nbsp;</p>",
